BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BFA Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T160000
UID:2604179oj5a-BoOkCJS5MTV1p6mg
DESCRIPTION:Each spring\, the University Art Gallery proudly presents the 
 Bachelor of Fine Arts \\(BFA\\) Exhibition\, showcasing the work of Sonoma
  State University's graduating BFA class. The 2026 BFA Exhibition will be 
 on view April 23-May 23\, 2026. Offered by SSU's Art Department\, the BFA 
 degree is distinguished from the BA by its rigorous\, studio-intensive cur
 riculum. The program requires an additional year of focused study\, includ
 ing advanced coursework in studio art\, art history\, and art theory. Ofte
 n regarded as the degree of choice for students pursuing graduate or profe
 ssional studies\, the BFA fosters significant artistic development within 
 a concentrated creative environment. For both students and faculty\, this 
 exhibition represents a culminating achievement-an opportunity to present 
 a carefully curated selection of each artist's strongest work in a profess
 ional gallery setting\, exhibited alongside their peers. Opening Reception
 : Thursday\, April 23\, 2026 4:00-6:00 pm
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/bfa-exhibition/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vallejo Hiking Club's Inaugural Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T113000
UID:2605169vG3pj8O00i2hUEFZysrqQ
DESCRIPTION:It's our first Vallejo Hiking Club hike! Part of our mission i
 s to take pride in Vallejo's green spaces\, and what better way to do that
  than enjoy them. We'll be hosting hikes along Vallejo's amazing trails ev
 ery month. Our goal is to get outside\, experience Vallejo's natural beaut
 y\, and perhaps introduce some less well known areas to the community.  
 \n\nWHERE: San Pablo Bay Hiking Trail on Mare Island\n\nWHAT: ~3.5 miles o
 ut and back hike\n\nWHEN: 10am start\, about an hour and a half of walking
  time. We aim to make these hikes family friendly and we'll try and give y
 ou a good idea of the "difficulty" of each hike in advance. We're also try
 ing to make these pretty short and manageable for everyone.\n\nDo you have
  a good idea for a hike? Want to host your own as a guide? Let us know!!
LOCATION:Mare Island San Pablo Bay Hiking Trail
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/vallejo-hiking-club-hosted-by-rooted-vall
 ejo-tickets-1989263069390
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
