BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Event: Pulling Stone by James Conaway
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T180000
UID:260512ZN_U5_myvEOxrb5ManpwCQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special event with James Conaway\, author of Pul
 ling Stone. This event is free\, but we appreciate your RSVP below so we c
 an plan for your attendance. ABOUT THE BOOK "Jim Conaway's diverse talents
  are manifest here in poems\, paintings and pottery\, in a muscular melang
 e for the soul and the senses. Whether luminous or flinty\, these works ar
 e wrought from a reverence for inner and outer wilderness." — Meredith D
 avis Hadaway\, author of the book\, "Among the Many Disappearing Things" a
 nd other works of poetry ABOUT THE AUTHOR James Conaway is the author of s
 even novels including The Big Easy \\(Houghton\\) and Nose \\(St. Martin
 ’s\\)\, a memoir\, Memphis Afternoons \\(Houghton\\)\, and the travel bo
 oks The Kingdom in the Country \\(Houghton\\) and Vanishing America \\(Cou
 nterpoint\\). His many books of nonfiction include Napa: The Story of an A
 merican Eden \\(Houghton\\)\, a bestseller\, and two sequels\, The Far Sid
 e of Eden \\(Houghton\\) and Napa at Last Light \\(Simon & Schuster\\). Hi
 s articles have appeared in The New York Times Magazine\, The Atlantic\, H
 arper’s\, The New Republic\, Outside\, American Scholar\, Smithsonian\, 
 National Geographic and other publications. He has worked for the New Orle
 ans Times-Picayune\, the Rome Daily American\, and the Washington Post Sty
 le section. He has been a Stegner Fellow at Stanford\, an Alicia Patterson
  Fellow\, and the editor of the National Trust’s magazine\, Preservation
 .
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1503403974783116/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
