BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Caldwell Snyder Gallery Exhibition Featuring Gilles Marrey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T170000
UID:260518vtprB-gzq0Kl8qPnAMUbZA
DESCRIPTION:Caldwell Snyder Gallery is pleased to present *Between Day & 
 Night*\, an exhibition of new works by acclaimed Parisian painter Gilles M
 arrey\, on display from May 30th – June 21st at the gallery’s historic
  Star Building location in St. Helena. Known for his atmospheric depiction
 s of contemporary life\, Marrey transforms familiar interiors\, urban stre
 etscapes\, and landscapes into emotionally resonant scenes through luminou
 s palettes of violets\, blues\, pinks\, and warm oranges. His paintings in
 vite viewers to slow down and reconsider everyday environments with renewe
 d attention and sensitivity.\n\nInfluenced by years of travel throughout t
 he Bay Area and inspired in part by the work of Richard Diebenkorn\, Marre
 y’s practice explores the relationship between structure\, light\, atmos
 phere\, and lived experience. Trained in France during the 1980s\, he deve
 loped a distinctive figurative style rooted in observation while remaining
  deeply contemporary in feeling and execution. Set within the heart of Nap
 a Valley\, the exhibition offers visitors an opportunity to experience Mar
 rey’s richly layered works in an intimate gallery setting while celebrat
 ing the intersection of contemporary art\, place\, and atmosphere.\n\n1328
  Main St\, St Helena\, CA 94574\n\n707.200.5050\n\nMonday – Saturday 10a
 m – 5pm\n\nSunday 11am – 5pm
LOCATION:Caldwell Snyder Gallery
URL:https://www.caldwellsnyder.com/artists/gilles-marrey
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Caldwell Snyder Artist Reception: Between Day & Night by Gilles Ma
 rrey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T180000
UID:260518kbJtD8Fzp0WSjmXGFmpE6g
DESCRIPTION:Caldwell Snyder Gallery is pleased to present *Between Day & 
 Night*\, an exhibition of new works by acclaimed Parisian painter Gilles M
 arrey\, with an opening reception on Saturday\, May 30th from 4:00–6:00 
 PM at the gallery’s historic Star Building location in St. Helena. Known
  for his atmospheric depictions of contemporary life\, Marrey transforms f
 amiliar interiors\, urban streetscapes\, and landscapes into emotionally r
 esonant scenes through luminous palettes of violets\, blues\, pinks\, and 
 warm oranges. His paintings invite viewers to slow down and reconsider eve
 ryday environments with renewed attention and sensitivity.\n\nInfluenced b
 y years of travel throughout the Bay Area and inspired in part by the work
  of Richard Diebenkorn\, Marrey’s practice explores the relationship bet
 ween structure\, light\, atmosphere\, and lived experience. Trained in Fra
 nce during the 1980s\, he developed a distinctive figurative style rooted 
 in observation while remaining deeply contemporary in feeling and executio
 n. Set within the heart of Napa Valley\, the exhibition offers visitors an
  opportunity to experience Marrey’s richly layered works in an intimate 
 gallery setting while celebrating the intersection of contemporary art\, p
 lace\, and atmosphere.\n\nFeaturing live music from jazz pop artist\, Clem
 on Charles and wine generously provided by V. Sattui Winery.\n\nAddress: 1
 328 Main St\, St Helena\, CA 94574\n\n707.200.5050\n\nMonday – Saturday 
 10am – 5pm\n\nSunday 11am – 5pm
LOCATION:Caldwell Snyder Gallery
URL:http://www.caldwellsnyder.com/artists/gilles-marrey
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
