BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Summertime Livin' Easy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T180000
UID:260519yMD0cnByWE-YfDYiQdM5Fw
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  5/15/26\n\n**JUNE EXHIBIT: SUMME
 RTIME LIVIN’ EASY**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **June 1 – June 28\, 2026**\n\
 n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, June 6\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Nancy Gra
 y  and Gallery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show a
 nd the Gallery’s 29th anniversary.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery
 ’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Re
 freshments will feature the Gallery’s signature mocktail: Brushstroke Fi
 zz.**\n\nSonoma County artist\, **Nancy Gray\,** unveils new summer-inspir
 ed acrylic paintings that are a colorful expressive interpretation of the 
 region’s beauty.  Summer is the artist’s favorite season and it shows
 . Drawing inspiration from the French Fauvist tradition\, these works abou
 nd with interpretive color choices and bold brush work.  Non-literal colo
 r expression plays out in “Evening Shade” as backlit trees cast blue t
 endrils of shade dancing on a bed of reddish ground.  Sprinkled across a 
 carpet of golden yellow\, vibrant red poppies glow in “Sundrenched Splen
 dor\,”amplifying the heat of the midday sun.  Red poppies take on a dra
 matic contrasting role in “Lavender Fields Forever” as they play again
 st the purplish blues and lavenders of the fields and sky.  Inspired by t
 he landscape\, these works reinterpret it through emotion and memory.  
 “We are blessed to live amongst Sonoma’s breathtaking scenery – ever
 ywhere I look\, I see a painting\,” noted Gray.\n\nGray has had a lifelo
 ng passion for art.  A Texas native\, she loves living in wine country wi
 th its inspirational landscapes.  Along with the Fauvist painters\, early
  years vacationing on the Caribbean Coast and Belize influenced her bright
  color palette.  She began exhibiting her art in Houston in the early 90
 ’s and continued to focus on her painting after moving to Sonoma County.
   Gray exhibits regionally and has been a member of the Upstairs Art Gall
 ery for five years.\n\nMeet the artist: Gray will host the Gallery on June
  18 and 25 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features
  **Collective Expressions: 29 Years\,** a members’ collaborative show ce
 lebrating the Gallery’s 29th anniversary. Gallery artists offer an excit
 ing mix of mediums\, subject matter and styles emblematic of the Gallery
 ’s dynamic diversity.  Landscapes by Barretta\, Laland\, and Zorich hig
 hlight our region’s beauty\; travel afar with Bird’s Paris cityscape\;
  from sunflowers to roses\, flowers star in works by Gray\, Haley\, Miller
 \, Schaffer\, Sumner and Wilson\; succulent oranges are the focus of Stolp
 er’s stunning still-life\; lovable pets are the subject of Tobin-Charles
 ton’s jewelry\; abstracts by Morgan and Reid bring a moving contemporary
  complement\; figurative works by Rapp\, Roney and Shore round out this cl
 assic to contemporary overview of the Upstairs artistic family.\n\nAlso jo
 in us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, June 4\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART 
 NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community ev
 ent celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating. 
  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Hea
 ldsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **ww
 w.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly 
 Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:4
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T193000
UID:260519pUxDAAnVGUOcxQcPyCRHCw
DESCRIPTION:JUNE 2 – JUNE 23\n\nFeel the Rhythm with Cumbia\n\nReady to 
 master the “Step of the Soul”? Join us for a high-energy cumbia class 
 where we dive into the heart of Latin America’s most infectious dance. W
 hether you have two left feet or you’re a dance floor regular\, this cla
 ss will get you moving with confidence.\n\nMireille will guide you through
 :\n\n4-Week Beginner Cumbia Series Program\n\nWeek 1 – Foundations & Rhy
 thm\n\n• Introduction to cumbia music and timing\n\n• Basic steps \\( 
 tropical and sonidera basics \\)\n\n• Understanding the beat \\( quick q
 uick slow – quick quick slow \\)\n\n• Intro to partner connection \\(c
 losed/open hold\\)\n\n⸻\n\nWeek 2 – Footwork Development \\+ cumbia Ba
 sic Turns\n\n• Review of basic step\n\n• Cumbia prep for turns\n\n• 
 Traveling basics \\(moving around the floor\\)\n\n• Intro to basic cumbi
 a turns .\n\n• Partner timing and frame basics\, partner work combinatio
 n.\n\n⸻\n\nWeek 3 – Styling & Partner Patterns\n\n• Review turns\n\n
 • Adding simple styling \\(arm movement\, body rhythm\\)\n\n• Cross-bo
 dy lead variation \\(beginner-friendly\\)\n\n• Smooth transitions betwee
 n moves\n\n. Partner work combination.\n\n⸻\n\nWeek 4 – Putting It All
  Together\n\n• Review all footwork and patterns\n\n• Combining moves i
 nto a short sequence\n\n• Musicality: dancing with the music\n\n• Conf
 idence and flow on the dance floor\n\n• Social dancing practice \\+ mini
  recap\n\nImportant Details\n\n• No dance experience required: Whether y
 ou’ve never danced before or it’s been a while\, you’re welcome here
 !\n\n• No partner necessary: Come solo or bring a friend—either way\, 
 you’ll have plenty of opportunities to dance.\n\n• Please wear non-mar
 king shoe soles: This helps us keep our dance floor in great condition.\n\
 nCome join us and discover the joy of cumbia. We can’t wait to see you o
 n the dance floor.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays \, 6:30 pm\n\n4 week course JU
 NE 2 – JUNE 23\n\nInstructor: Mireille Ruiz Born and raised in Mexico Ci
 ty\, she grew up dancing and listening to Latin Music as part of her cultu
 re including Cumbia\, Banda\, ranchera\, quebradita\, etc.\n\nshe learned 
 her first following Techniques\, dancing with her father in every family f
 iesta.\n\nshe has a background in Mexican folklore\, Jazz\, tap dancing an
 d gymnastics\, she also is a percussionist\, drummer and Montessori Teache
 r.\n\nShe grew up performing since she the age of 4. Bay Area bachata and 
 cumbia dance instructor\, Mireille has been teaching dance\, performing\, 
 leading dance teams\, around USA events\, dance festivals\, congresses sin
 ce 2008\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arr
 ive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/cumbia/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tuesdays in the Plaza: Ariel Marin Band (Funk / Soul / Motown)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T200000
UID:260518nK2sWddYCUmkGmx4W1dKBA
DESCRIPTION:Our weekly summer concerts in the Healdsburg Plaza from 6:00 p
 .m. to 8:00 p.m. provide an eclectic and unique line-up of bands\, and hav
 e been assembled to please a wide array of musical interests. Food vendors
  will be on-hand to offer locally sourced food for sale starting at 5:00 p
 .m. with the music beginning at 6:00 p.m.\n\nAbout the band: Ariel Marin i
 s a refreshingly eclectic inspirational singer with an angelic voice. Havi
 ng grown up in the San Francisco Bay Area\, she was exposed to a melting p
 ot of cultures. As a result\, her unique music is heavily influenced by a 
 of multitude of styles including folk\, rock\, r&b\, gospel\, classical\, 
 and pop to name a few. Her mother having been a professional rock singer\,
  Ariel spent much of her childhood around recording artists including the 
 Dinosaurs\, Tony Saunders\, Arlo Guthrie\, and the Grateful Dead. Her song
 s come straight from the heart and speak to the depths of the soul.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza
URL:https://healdsburg.gov/335/Tuesdays-in-the-Plaza
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T170000
UID:260508HlPBJzDWl0yKonp95AXlKw
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Melvin Seals and JGB
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T000000
UID:2604169TRXWdTaokS0pX4qo40V4w
DESCRIPTION:Melvin Seals has been a powerful presence in the music industr
 y for over 30 years with a long-established reputation as a performer\, re
 cording artist and producer. Melvin is most revered for his powerful\, hig
 h-spirited\, Hammond B-3 organ\, and keyboards in the Jerry Garcia Band. M
 elvin spun his B-3 magic with the Jerry Garcia Band for 18 years and in do
 ing so helped pioneer and define what has now become "Jam Band Music". Fro
 m blues to funk to rock to jazz\, Melvin Seals serves up a tasty mix with 
 a little R&B and gospel thrown in to spice things up.  \n\nMelvin and JGB 
 bring an intuitive\, expressive style\, soul\, spontaneity and remarkable 
 chops to the table. John Kadlecik on lead guitar and vocal duties\, John-P
 aul McLean's savory bass\, Pete Lavezzoli’s hearty drums and\, of course
 \, a heapin' helpin' of the wizard's magic on Hammond B-3 Organ and keyboa
 rds. Along with Lady Chi & Mary-eL on back-up vocals\, the result is a mos
 t satisfying blend of natural organic grooves that challenges genre bounda
 ries. Their chemistry is the focus from which they create a spontaneous an
 d high art where the sky is the limit musically. They offer an exciting\, 
 often psychedelic musical journey that changes nightly and keeps the audie
 nce dancing and smiling \\(and some staring in amazement\\) for hours.  \n
 \nAdding his rock-gospel-soul-rhythm and blues touch with his funky style 
 of playing\, no wonder Jerry nicknamed him "Master of the Universe". Melvi
 n continues to treat music lovers to his unique brand of melodic flavor wi
 th JGB. Come see and hear for yourself!  \n\nMELVIN SEALS & JGB:  \n\nMelv
 in Seals - Hammond B3 Organ\, Keyboards & Vocals  \n\nJohn Kadlecik - Elec
 tric Guitar & Lead Vocals \n\nJohn-Paul McLean - Bass \n\nPete Lavezzoli -
  Drums  \n\nLady Chi & Mary-eL - Backup Vocals
LOCATION:The Junction Beer Garden
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108208846?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The World of Kabbalah begins April 21
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T193000
UID:260414-TNT5cUdIE6Yy6ESWkr2oA
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever been curious about Kabbalah\, but unsure what it
  really is?\n\nChabad of Novato invites the community to join a new six-we
 ek course: The World of Kabbalah.\n\nThis engaging course will explore Ju
 daism’s deeper mystical teachings in a clear\, thoughtful\, and practica
 l way\, offering insight into the soul\, purpose\, inner growth\, and the 
 deeper meaning of life.\n\nClasses will be held on Tuesdays at 7:30 PM o
 n April 21\, 28\, May 12\, 19\, 26\, and June 2.\n\nThe course is open to
  both in-person and online participants. In-person classes will take plac
 e at Chabad of Novato\, 695 De Long Ave\, Novato. A Zoom option is avai
 lable\, and recordings will be emailed to participants in case they miss
  a live class.\n\nCost: $99\, including textbook. No previous background i
 s needed.\n\nTo register or learn more\, visit jewishnovato.com/jlikabbala
 h For questions\, contact Rabbi Menachem Landa at rabbi@JewishNovato.co
 m or 415-878-6770
LOCATION:Chabad Jewish Center of Novato
URL:https://www.jewishnovato.com/templates/articlecco_cdo/aid/7294661/jewi
 sh/The-World-of-Kabbalah.htm
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Salsa - Tuesdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T183000
UID:260319RlKCQWt8sECuLTG6-j14NA
DESCRIPTION:Ready to dance? Join our beginner salsa class where no experie
 nce or partner is needed. Just comfortable shoes and desire to have fun!\n
 \nGreat for first timers!\n\nNo dance experience required\n\nNon-marking s
 hoes soles\n\nNo partner necessary\n\nOur relaxed environment is perfect f
 or learning salsa basics\, as we make it fun and enjoyable. In this class 
 you will learn basic directional steps\, proper frame for partner-work and
  simple turn patterns. We organize our curriculum so that the movements ar
 e easy to remember. Join us to learn the fundamentals! No experience is ne
 cessary and no partner is required. Drop-in fee is $20.\n\nDate & Time: Tu
 esdays @ 5:30PM – 6:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/beginner-salsa-tuesdays
 /17157360/2026-06-02T17
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T193000
UID:260318RZ2Xjf_K0EmTwOlbo3yT4w
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\nPre- requisite:\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach week\,
  we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connection 
 that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go beyond 
 the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate pat
 terns and styling\, including:\n\nTurns and Spins:\n\nMaster your inside a
 nd outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Toss moves.
 \n\nIntricate Patterns:\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, as well as va
 rious Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n\nFootwork a
 nd Styling:\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced footwork like t
 he Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work on styling with 
 a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.\n\nThis class i
 s your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead-follow connecti
 on\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your salsa vocabulary. 
 Join us and elevate your dance!\n\nDetails:\n\nNo partner necessary — ro
 tations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe so
 les to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get s
 ettled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 6:30PM – 7:30PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/intermediate-salsa-clas
 s/17159571/2026-06-02T18
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ellie James Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260602T000000
UID:26022465e6oHzD3UamCR4oixwgUg
DESCRIPTION:Your new favorite song is just around the corner. Enter the wo
 rld of singer-songwriter and producer Ellie James\, and treat yourself to 
 a show unlike any you've ever seen. Stylistically unique and captivating\,
  Ellie James mixes lush indie-pop sounds with the style and edge of her ro
 ck ’n’ roll background. Her music is both genuine and dance-inducing\,
  as she uses real instruments and electronic production to weave musical s
 tories all her own. Ellie has been performing professionally all over the 
 world for more than 10 years\, most recently opening up for Grammy-winning
  artist Colbie Caillat\, and playing to electric audiences at Hollywood’
 s famous Viper Room and San Francisco’s Cafe du Nord. With the release o
 f her much-anticipated sophomore EP “Favorite Stranger” and a nearly s
 old-out headlining show at Hopmonk\, Ellie shows no signs of stopping with
  a year ahead full of new shows\, new merch\, and new music.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107729871?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
