DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260605T210000
UID:260517j0HvZuxCD0KTKLKZA48vFg
DESCRIPTION:First Fridays Salsa series\, don’t miss out! Get ready to ge
 t loose and move your body at our First Fridays Salsa Party under the star
 s!  At 7pm\, we’re serving up a sizzling dance class featuring Salsa\, M
 erengue\, Dancehall\, Afrobeats\, and more—it’s like a dance buffet fo
 r your feet!  Open dancing begins at 6pm and follows the dance lesson unti
 l 9pm.  Brace yourself for double the DJ magic with DJ Jay Fresco and B\\_
 Elev8ed spinning a mix of Latin and Afro beats that'll keep you grooving a
 ll night. \\*\\*Clear your calendar and come have some fun!\\*\\* Venue De
 tails | Parking | Entrance: This event will be held in our backyard venue\
 , dress accordingly as it might get chilly. We are located at the corner o
 f Walnut Ave and Kansas Street on Mare Island. There is plenty of parking 
 on the street and in gravel lots on Kansas Street. Event entrance will be 
 at our side driveway gate on Kansas Street.  Food & Beverage: You're welco
 me to bring your own picnic dinner\, water\, and any nonalcoholic beverage
 s. A variety of snacks and wine will be available for purchase.  \\*NO out
 side alcohol of any kind is permitted.  Misc: We are family friendly!  Min
 ors welcome. Well mannered/managed doggies are welcome in the outside venu
 e area. There is plenty of seating\, we will have tables and chairs for ev
 eryone.  And if you prefer\, your own comfy chairs and blankets are welcom
 e.  Time:  Gate opens at 5:30pm\, open dancing starts at 6pm\, lessons at 
 7pm\, and open dancing to follow until 9pm.  TICKETS ARE $20 IF PURCHASED 
 ONLINE TICKETS ARE $25 IF PURCHASED AT THE DOOR
LOCATION:Vino Godfather
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1611135219996152/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Talking about Venus at Robert Ferguson Observatory
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260605T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260605T223000
UID:260516uF2qVTqNIkCvynX9NolCVA
DESCRIPTION:Discover the beauty and mystery of Venus during this special F
 ocus Night exploring one of the brightest and most fascinating planets in 
 our solar system. The evening begins with an engaging presentation coverin
 g Venus's thick cloud cover\, extreme surface temperatures\, runaway green
 house effect\, and its importance in astronomy and human history. Guests w
 ill also learn how ancient civilizations tracked Venus across the sky and 
 how modern space missions have revealed more about the planet's hidden sur
 face. After the presentation\, visitors can observe Venus through the obse
 rvatory's telescopes\, watching its changing phases as it moves through th
 e solar system. Perfect for both beginners and experienced stargazers\, th
 is immersive evening offers a deeper understanding of our brilliant neighb
 oring planet.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/talking-about-venus-at-robert-ferguson-ob
 servatory/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
