BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flynn Creek Circus - The Cricket and the Wren
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T170000
UID:260519XWUclpnD7kq44cgbLU478A
DESCRIPTION:Flynn Creek Circus Presents ‘The Cricket & the Wren’: a hi
 ghly original\, all-human circus that enchants through breathtaking acroba
 tics and athletically stunning skill. Sponsored by the Circus Mentors Inc 
 501c3.\n\nWindsor\, CA— June 11 - 14– This 2026 season\, Flynn Creek C
 ircus invites audiences to ‘The Cricket & the Wren’ — memorable fami
 ly fun and Artful athleticism under the circus big top.\n\nA merchant’s 
 daughter sets out to find the castle where the horizon meets the sea. In o
 rder to  break the spell of the Frog Prince\, she must brave a harrowing 
 journey filled with wonder.\n\nAlong the adventure\, she encounters Jack a
 nd the Beanstalk’s sassy cow\, an out of pocket Pirate and the secret sa
 crifice of the cricket and the wren. \n\nFeaturing aerialists\, jugglers\
 , knife throwers\, and laugh out loud comedy\, this circus blends classic 
 storybook archetypes with imaginative new heroes. The Cricket and the Wren
  will surprise\, dazzle and delight all ages. \n\nIn addition to the fami
 ly friendly showings\,  and the interactive children's camp program held 
 under the circus big top\,  Flynn Creek Circus also presents the wildly p
 opular 'Adults Only Show' boasting outrageous acts\, dark comedy\, and an 
 infamous party atmosphere. Check the website for select adults only showti
 mes as well as special discount nights.\n\nSpectators for all showings are
  invited to the tent to experience the magic up to 30 minutes before each 
 show. The event will offer beer\, wine\, and light concession for purchase
  and include a 15 minute intermission during the two hour show.\n\nLimited
  free parking is available at the location at Keiser Park. \n\nTickets fo
 r Flynn Creek Circus are now available for purchase online at flynncreekci
 rcus.com. Individual ticket prices start at $27 or\, for table reservation
 s\, options start at $98 for two attendees. \n\nFind showtimes and more d
 etails on the camp programs for ages 5-8 and 7-15 at flynncreekcircus.com\
 n\nEarly booking is encouraged for this highly anticipated event.
LOCATION:Keiser Park- Under the Big Top Tent
URL:https://flynncreekcircus.ticketspice.com/2026-windsor-cricket-wren
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Transforming the Judgmental Mind
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T160000
UID:2605198oOKOpXQPkGndx2lMVbu5w
DESCRIPTION:with Donald Rothberg\n\nJudgments of a reactive and compulsive
  nature\, both toward ourselves and toward others\, are very strong in mos
 t of our lives. They can distort our perceptions\, make relationships with
  others difficult\, and undermine our work. We will examine what judgments
  are and how to work with them\, using mindfulness\, heart practices\, and
  inquiry—preserving the discernment they can offer while working through
  their destructive aspects. We will also explore how we internalize the ju
 dgments of our society in a number of ways\, particularly related to race\
 , gender\, sexual orientation\, etc. Attendees will have the option of reg
 ular follow-up sessions to continue and deepen the learning.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/transforming-the-judgm
 ental-mind-dr2d26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flynn Creek Circus - The Cricket and the Wren
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T210000
UID:2605193FaPyB66kkKYvFyNJ3J80w
DESCRIPTION:Flynn Creek Circus Presents ‘The Cricket & the Wren’: a hi
 ghly original\, all-human circus that enchants through breathtaking acroba
 tics and athletically stunning skill. Sponsored by the Circus Mentors Inc 
 501c3.\n\nWindsor\, CA— June 11 - 14– This 2026 season\, Flynn Creek C
 ircus invites audiences to ‘The Cricket & the Wren’ — memorable fami
 ly fun and Artful athleticism under the circus big top.\n\nA merchant’s 
 daughter sets out to find the castle where the horizon meets the sea. In o
 rder to  break the spell of the Frog Prince\, she must brave a harrowing 
 journey filled with wonder.\n\nAlong the adventure\, she encounters Jack a
 nd the Beanstalk’s sassy cow\, an out of pocket Pirate and the secret sa
 crifice of the cricket and the wren. \n\nFeaturing aerialists\, jugglers\
 , knife throwers\, and laugh out loud comedy\, this circus blends classic 
 storybook archetypes with imaginative new heroes. The Cricket and the Wren
  will surprise\, dazzle and delight all ages. \n\nIn addition to the fami
 ly friendly showings\,  and the interactive children's camp program held 
 under the circus big top\,  Flynn Creek Circus also presents the wildly p
 opular 'Adults Only Show' boasting outrageous acts\, dark comedy\, and an 
 infamous party atmosphere. Check the website for select adults only showti
 mes as well as special discount nights.\n\nSpectators for all showings are
  invited to the tent to experience the magic up to 30 minutes before each 
 show. The event will offer beer\, wine\, and light concession for purchase
  and include a 15 minute intermission during the two hour show.\n\nLimited
  free parking is available at the location at Keiser Park. \n\nTickets fo
 r Flynn Creek Circus are now available for purchase online at flynncreekci
 rcus.com. Individual ticket prices start at $27 or\, for table reservation
 s\, options start at $98 for two attendees. \n\nFind showtimes and more d
 etails on the camp programs for ages 5-8 and 7-15 at flynncreekcircus.com\
 n\nEarly booking is encouraged for this highly anticipated event.
LOCATION:Keiser Park- Under the Big Top Tent
URL:https://flynncreekcircus.ticketspice.com/2026-windsor-cricket-wren
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Summertime Livin' Easy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T180000
UID:2605192mg6wYOpAkW0PxkUtunTzw
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  5/15/26\n\n**JUNE EXHIBIT: SUMME
 RTIME LIVIN’ EASY**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **June 1 – June 28\, 2026**\n\
 n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, June 6\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Nancy Gra
 y  and Gallery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show a
 nd the Gallery’s 29th anniversary.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery
 ’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Re
 freshments will feature the Gallery’s signature mocktail: Brushstroke Fi
 zz.**\n\nSonoma County artist\, **Nancy Gray\,** unveils new summer-inspir
 ed acrylic paintings that are a colorful expressive interpretation of the 
 region’s beauty.  Summer is the artist’s favorite season and it shows
 . Drawing inspiration from the French Fauvist tradition\, these works abou
 nd with interpretive color choices and bold brush work.  Non-literal colo
 r expression plays out in “Evening Shade” as backlit trees cast blue t
 endrils of shade dancing on a bed of reddish ground.  Sprinkled across a 
 carpet of golden yellow\, vibrant red poppies glow in “Sundrenched Splen
 dor\,”amplifying the heat of the midday sun.  Red poppies take on a dra
 matic contrasting role in “Lavender Fields Forever” as they play again
 st the purplish blues and lavenders of the fields and sky.  Inspired by t
 he landscape\, these works reinterpret it through emotion and memory.  
 “We are blessed to live amongst Sonoma’s breathtaking scenery – ever
 ywhere I look\, I see a painting\,” noted Gray.\n\nGray has had a lifelo
 ng passion for art.  A Texas native\, she loves living in wine country wi
 th its inspirational landscapes.  Along with the Fauvist painters\, early
  years vacationing on the Caribbean Coast and Belize influenced her bright
  color palette.  She began exhibiting her art in Houston in the early 90
 ’s and continued to focus on her painting after moving to Sonoma County.
   Gray exhibits regionally and has been a member of the Upstairs Art Gall
 ery for five years.\n\nMeet the artist: Gray will host the Gallery on June
  18 and 25 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features
  **Collective Expressions: 29 Years\,** a members’ collaborative show ce
 lebrating the Gallery’s 29th anniversary. Gallery artists offer an excit
 ing mix of mediums\, subject matter and styles emblematic of the Gallery
 ’s dynamic diversity.  Landscapes by Barretta\, Laland\, and Zorich hig
 hlight our region’s beauty\; travel afar with Bird’s Paris cityscape\;
  from sunflowers to roses\, flowers star in works by Gray\, Haley\, Miller
 \, Schaffer\, Sumner and Wilson\; succulent oranges are the focus of Stolp
 er’s stunning still-life\; lovable pets are the subject of Tobin-Charles
 ton’s jewelry\; abstracts by Morgan and Reid bring a moving contemporary
  complement\; figurative works by Rapp\, Roney and Shore round out this cl
 assic to contemporary overview of the Upstairs artistic family.\n\nAlso jo
 in us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, June 4\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART 
 NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community ev
 ent celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating. 
  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Hea
 ldsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **ww
 w.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly 
 Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
