BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley Pride
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T220000
UID:26051503LL9qFIR0uv53489eIlsg
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma Valley Pride returns for a full weekend of queer joy\, 
 live entertainment\, community\, and Pride in the heart of Sonoma Valley.\
 n\nThis year’s celebration expands into a three-day Pride weekend\, brin
 ging together music\, drag\, dancing\, local artists\, food\, wine\, commu
 nity organizations\, and LGBTQIA+ visibility across Sonoma. Sonoma Valley 
 Pride is focused on building queer spaces\, creating joyful gathering plac
 es\, and bringing more LGBTQIA+ entertainment and community-centered progr
 amming to the region.\n\nThe weekend kicks off Friday\, June 12\, with **W
 e Rise With Pride**\, Sonoma Valley Pride’s first annual Concert and Dra
 g Show at the historic Sebastiani Theatre. The evening features headliner 
 **J. Graves**\, a queer\, non-binary-led band from Portland known for thei
 r guitar-driven sound\, bold vocals\, and high-energy live performances. B
 lending dance-punk\, post-punk\, and garage rock influences\, J. Graves br
 ings a sound that will appeal to fans of **Yeah Yeah Yeahs** and **The Kil
 ls** — rhythmic\, electric\, and built for the stage. The night also fea
 tures drag from Bay Area legends **Kochina Rude**\, Sonoma County native\,
  host\, and performer\, and **Tila Pia**\, an infamous stunt queen who has
  turned looks from Hawaii to New York.\n\nOn Saturday\, June 13\, the cele
 bration continues with a Pride Dance Party at **The General’s Daughter**
 \, inviting the community to keep the weekend moving with music\, dancing\
 , and celebration.\n\nOn Sunday\, June 14\, Sonoma Valley Pride gathers on
  the historic Sonoma Plaza for a free community Pride Festival featuring l
 ive performances\, speakers\, queer art\, local vendors\, food\, wine\, an
 d community connection. With a bigger stage\, more room to gather\, and ev
 en more ways to celebrate\, the Plaza Festival is designed for friends\, f
 amilies\, chosen families\, locals\, visitors\, and allies to come togethe
 r in the spirit of Pride.\n\nFrom the theatre to the dance floor to the Pl
 aza lawn\, Sonoma Valley Pride weekend is a celebration of queer artistry\
 , visibility\, belonging\, and joy in Sonoma Valley. Come ready to dance\,
  show up\, and be part of what comes next.
LOCATION:Sonoma Plaza
URL:https://www.sonomavalleypride.com/?utm_source=bohemian&utm_medium=soci
 al&utm_campaign=pride-weekend---2026-svp-pride-festival-&utm_content=svp--
 -bohemian
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack London Speaker Series: Tarnel Abbott - Jack's Great Granddaug
 hter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T120000
UID:260513SAiMSssqu0moMPgBjEECiQ
DESCRIPTION:Jack London’s great-granddaughter Tarnel Abbott will speak i
 n an interview format presentation. A retired librarian who spent 22 years
  at the Richmond Public Library\, Abbott has dedicated herself to preservi
 ng London’s books and papers. She is also a longtime activist\, involved
  in numerous local and international causes\, and will share her insights 
 into London’s life and legacy.\n\nShe will be interviewed by Gail Yamamo
 to Seymour\, an environmental scientist and advocate for endangered specie
 s\, climate change adaptation\, and environmental justice. She is a third 
 generation Californian Japanese American.  Over the past 50 years\, Seymo
 ur has been a self-educated follower of Jack London’s history\, drawn to
  his adventurous lifestyle and humanitarian ideologies.  Gail treasures h
 er friendship with Tarnel Abbott\, Jack London’s great granddaughter\, b
 ecause like her great grandfather and grandmother\, she is genuinely compa
 ssionate and is a vocal activist promoting justice for all.\n\nThis is par
 t of a quarterly speaker series\, co-presented by the Jack London Society 
 and Jack London Park Partners\, in honor of Jack London’s 150th birthday
  year.  The series features a range of experts and scholars\, sharing ins
 ights into Jack London’s life\, work\, and legacy and his connections to
  literature\, photography\, and the Bay Area.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/jl-speaker-series-tarnel-abbott/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Disco Dance Party 2026 - Rainbow Edition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T220000
UID:260513Ola5OiU7skyDsqLiD5JnXg
DESCRIPTION:DJ Rotten Robbie will be spinning an all-vinyl\, all-disco set
 \, and guests will help pick the records.  Guests disinclined toward dan
 cing can walk the red carpet to a VIP photo nook and enjoy a smorgasbord o
 f 1970’s and 80’s-themed treats. It’s after hours. It’s late night
  (for Napa Valley\, anyway). It’s a little dry\, full of flavor\, and fa
 ted to be fabulous! \n\nCharbay Distillery will be pouring its classic cl
 ear vodka for dry martinis\, while the sobriety-curious will have plenty t
 o enjoy with brightly flavored mocktails from Mother Root. Guests can knoc
 k back a "shooter" containing a delicious oyster from Osprey Seafood\, swi
 mming in a bubbling sea of Bloody Mary mix\, and sample some of the delica
 cies that made the 1970s and 80's so memorable -- a culinary era notable f
 or its Crock Pots\, mini gherkins\, pigs in blankets and fondue.  \n\nGu
 ests are encouraged to fully embrace the era\, by making their own playlis
 t of favorite Disco tunes\, putting on their best Boogie Shoes\, and donni
 ng their Disco Duds - outfits inspired by the era -- from velour bell-bott
 oms\, unbuttoned Quiana shirts\, shimmery sequin jumpsuits\, glittery eye 
 shadow and mood rings\, or “Bee Gees” white polyester suits. Chest hai
 r and gold chains are optional. Whether your style is John Travolta or Zig
 gy Stardust\, Donna Summer or Cher\, and whether you rock a mullet\, “gl
 itter fro” or shag\, you are sure to catch a sizzling case of Saturday
  Night Fever.
LOCATION:Napa Valley Museum
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/products/dry-ish-january-disco-dance-part
 y-2026-at-the-mac
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
