DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T150000
UID:260511H4RYDyeOTEChgRrQU-r7TQ
DESCRIPTION:Meet\, watch\, and talk to Ignatz-nominated interdisciplinary 
 artist and educator Mara Ramirez\, whose work ruminates on the body in sp
 ace through metaphor\, fantasy\, and realism alike. Bending images of biol
 ogical life\, the stories they tell range in content\, from poetic meditat
 ions on gender to funny and sad character studies in cartoon formats. Rami
 rez is the creator of Flea \\(2025 Fieldmouse Press\\)\, as well as many
  short runs of poetry comics from Floss Editions\, Irrelevant Press\, and 
 \\(self-published\\) Freak Comics.\n\nA lifelong zinester and Esnupi lover
 \, Ramirez will be sharing a make-your-own mini-zine project!
LOCATION:Charles M. Schulz Museum
URL:https://schulzmuseum.org/mara-ramirez/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SugarShuttle: Sugarloaf ↔ Hood Mtn\, Pythian Rd—CA State Parks
  Week
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T110000
UID:260511A59y0FwrcEaokN3hEFeFKg
DESCRIPTION:**How it works**: Every half hour\, our Shuttle will 
 leave from either Sugarloaf Ridge State Park's Visitor Center (ma
 king a brief stop at the Goodspeed parking lot) or Hood Mountai
 n Regional Park’s Pythian Rd parking lot (with a brief stop a
 t the equestrian lot). Make a reservation to ride to the other
  end of the trail and begin your hike\, or hike and ride back
 . We recommend riding first and hiking back to your car afterwa
 rd– no worries about how long you take to finish your adventu
 re. The hike should take 3½ to 4½ hours\; the distance is ab
 out 7.4 miles one-way with approximately 2\,300ft of elevation ga
 in. Bring at least 64 oz of water and sun protection\, as the
  majority of the trail is exposed. \n\nIf you are riding from 
 Sugarloaf\, the Goodspeed lot fills up quickly. If it is full\,
  please park at the main lot and pick up the shuttle at the 
 Visitor Center (you will have to hike a mile back to the main
  lot from the bottom of the canyon/Goodspeed lot). If the Hood
  Mt. Pythian Lot is full\, please park at the Equestrian Lot\,
  by the Hood House\, in Los Guilicos. \n\n**Registration is requ
 ired as there is only space for 5 riders at a time**\, but yo
 u can ride on a space-available basis as well. There is no cha
 rge for the ride\, the $10 reservation fee is refunded on site
  the day of the event\, unless you choose to donate it to kee
 p this service running. **Dogs and bikes are not allowed in the
  shuttle or on Goodspeed Trail** (the State Park portion of the
  hiking route). Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026spwk-satshuttle
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T170000
UID:260508ztp7nOQXBECVTEb1ZmDTbA
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
