BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GUIDE DOGS FOR THE BLIND'S GRADUATION CEREMONIES MELT HEARTS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T143000
UID:260314SSYUZIR2nE-l8q5_eNS9Dw
DESCRIPTION:Guide Dogs for the Blind \\(GDB\\) will celebrate its guide d
 og team graduates every other Saturday with public graduation ceremonies a
 t the organization’s campus in San Rafael. These touching public events 
 have inspired tears in even the most stoic audience members\, as graduatin
 g guide dog teams proudly take the stage. Families are welcome at the cere
 monies\, which honor the independence and companionship that GDB’s gui
 de dogs provide for GDB’s clients who are blind or visually impaired. T
 he events also allow GDB’s clients to meet the puppy raisers who cared 
 for their canine heroes prior to beginning formal training at GDB’s cam
 pus. Ceremonies also recognize recent graduates of GDB’s Orientation an
 d Mobility \\(O&M\\) Program\, K9 Buddy Program\, and Breeder Dog Program
 .\n\nAdmission is free\, and Kleenex will be provided. Pre-registered bus 
 groups are welcome. Public tours of the campus are offered on the days of 
 the ceremonies. Visit www.guidedogs.com for more information. Graduat
 ion events are also livestreamed at https://www.youtube.com/@gdb\\_offici
 al/streams.
LOCATION:Guide Dogs for the Blind
URL:https://www.guidedogs.com/about-guide-dogs-for-the-blind/graduations
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Press Democrat Presents North Coast Wine & Food Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T160000
UID:26022706Lijn-q0EGAsX2kEWrIqA
DESCRIPTION:Back to All Shows\n\nPress Democrat Presents\n\nNorth Coast Wi
 ne & Food Festival\n\nSaturday\, June 13\, 2026\n\n12:00 pm VIP Entry\n\n1
 :00 pm General Admission\n\nBUY TICKETS \n\nGet ready for a day of indulge
 nce\, discovery\, and celebration at the North Coast Wine & Food Festival\
 , the North Bay’s premier showcase of exceptional wines and culinary tal
 ent. The festival brings together gold-medal-winning wines from Sonoma\, N
 apa\, and Mendocino counties\, alongside inspired bites from some of the r
 egion’s most celebrated chefs. Guests are invited to sip\, savor\, and c
 onnect—meeting the winemakers behind the pours and tasting dishes that r
 eflect the rich agricultural and cultural diversity of the North Coast. \n
 \nFrom elegant caviar to bold barbecue and globally inspired flavors\, the
  culinary offerings are as diverse as they are delicious\, all complemente
 d by live music and the vibrant energy of wine country. As festival attend
 ee Dennis McCarter of McCarter Cellars shared\, “The great food at the e
 vent elevates the great wine\, and the great wine elevates the great food.
 ” Established as a must-attend event for food and wine lovers alike\, th
 e North Coast Wine & Food Festival is more than a tasting—it’s a joyfu
 l celebration of craftsmanship\, community\, and the good life. \n\nMust b
 e 21 or older to attend. \n\nDesignated driver tickets are available\, alo
 ng with a limited selection of non-alcoholic beverages. \n\n \n\n \n\nTHIR
 D PARTY RESELLERS\n\nDon’t get taken by deceptive online resellers who u
 se bots to buy tickets and then mark up their prices. The only safe way to
  protect your purchase and guarantee the best seats at the lowest cost is 
 to work directly with us: through our website\, by phone\, or at our box o
 ffice in Santa Rosa. Plus\, we’re not bots. Our friendly team members ar
 e easily accessible by phone or at the box office to provide customer supp
 ort.
